From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:29:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: command environments (ADDRESS) written in JavaScript

.js~addCommandEnvironment(name, fn) makes a JavaScript function, of any
realm, an ADDRESS environment; .js~removeCommandEnvironment(name) removes
it (the name then answers FAILURE RC 30, as an unknown environment; a
name with no handler is an error).  Built
on cmdhandler.cls: wasm/web/jscommands.cls, loaded by js.cls on first use,
has .JSCommandHandler, a .CommandHandler whose ~command calls
fn(command, ctx) on the Rexx thread that issued the command: what it returns
is RC (undefined or null: 0; a Promise is waited for), ctx the command's
.CommandContext as a RexxProxy whose tests (hasVar, isRedirected, isValid)
answer booleans; in the page its calls give Promises.  A JavaScript
exception is SYNTAX 98.900 where the command was issued (ADDITIONAL as for
any JavaScript exception); a condition of Rexx that the function lets
through is raised there as itself.  A handler of .nil, or anything but a
function, is SYNTAX 93.900.
- From the page (ooRexx.js): a session's addCommandEnvironment(name, fn)
  and removeCommandEnvironment(name) (.JSSession), and
  start({commandEnvironments: {NAME: fn}}).
- wasm/build-node.sh, wasm/build-web.sh: jscommands.cls next to js.cls.
- Tests: wasm/tests/js-commands.rex (34 checks, Node and the worker's
  realm; in qualify-node-cli.sh and web-api.py), web-api.py "js commands
  page" (a function of the page) and "session commands".
Not part of the posted RFE (it needs cmdhandler).
